Exceptions: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines gate exception (waiver) rules and management.

Waiver:
  Format: WAIVER-NNN

  Fields:
    Gate: <gate-id>
    Reason: <why waiver is needed>
    Owner: <who approved>
    Expiration: <datetime>
    Risk: <risk assessment>
    Approval: <approval authority>

WaiverRules:
  [WVR1] Waiver MUST have Reason, Owner, Expiration, Risk, Approval.
  [WVR2] Waiver is temporary; expired waivers re-trigger gate.
  [WVR3] Waiver does not bypass gate permanently.
  [WVR4] Waiver MUST be recorded in graph.

ExpiredWaiver:
  WAIVER-009
    ↓
  EXPIRED
    ↓
  Gate re-required

SkipVsWaive:
  SKIPPED:
    Gate not applicable to project
  WAIVED:
    Gate applicable but approved to skip

ExceptionRules:
  [EX1]  SKIPPED ≠ WAIVED.
  [EX2]  Waivers require explicit approval.
  [EX3]  Waivers have expiration dates.
  [EX4]  Expired waivers MUST be renewed or gate re-run.

State: +
  